FAWE-ButInMods
==============

This project is a clean-room *port* of the feature set and command surface of
FastAsyncWorldEdit (FAWE) and WorldEdit to the Fabric mod loader for
Minecraft 1.21.10, with no plugin/platform dependencies.

It reproduces:
  * the complete command surface of FastAsyncWorldEdit 2.x for Minecraft
    1.21.10 (WorldEdit 7.3.17 core commands + FAWE's additional commands),
  * FAWE's selection/mask/pattern/transform/brush/tool model,
  * FAWE's block/chunk data model (palette-packed chunk sections, bulk chunk
    queue, deferred "side effects" such as lighting updates, history recorded
    at chunk level),
  * the schematic formats (Sponge Schematic v1/v2/v3, legacy MCEdit .schematic,
    structure .nbt) with FAWE's clipboard semantics.

Reference upstream projects (both GPL-3.0):
  * FastAsyncWorldEdit — https://github.com/IntellectualSites/FastAsyncWorldEdit
      Copyright (C) IntellectualSites and contributors
  * WorldEdit          — https://github.com/EngineHub/WorldEdit
      Copyright (C) sk89q and contributors

The upstream sources were used as the behavioural specification: command names,
aliases, flags, argument lists, parser ids (masks/patterns/transforms), brush
and tool semantics and default configuration values are taken from them so that
FAWE users find exactly the same commands.  Internal code in this repository was
written for this project (no upstream source file is copied verbatim), therefore
no upstream file carries over its own authorship; the *behaviour* is derived
from the GPL-3.0 licensed upstream projects above and this project is licensed
GPL-3.0 as well (see LICENSE.txt).

Neither FastAsyncWorldEdit nor WorldEdit are required at runtime: the mod ships
its own engine.
